{"type":"message","id":"3b36b324","parentId":"b3e54b53","timestamp":"2026-05-19T02:32:14.919Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Cloudflare is returning a 500 error with \"error code: 1101\" for POST requests. This seems to be a Cloudflare Workers issue - the POST handler might be throwing an exception or the route might not be properly set up on the Workers side. The GET endpoints work fine, so the Workers itself is running, but the POST /send endpoint has an internal error.\n\nLet me try a few more variations to diagnose:\n\n1. Maybe the request body format is wrong\n2. Maybe the endpoint path is different\n3. Maybe I need to check what error 1101 means on Cloudflare Workers\n\nActually, error 1101 on Cloudflare Workers typically means \"Worker thrown an exception\" - so the Workers code itself has a bug when handling POST requests. This is a server-side issue.\n\n\nSince the POST endpoint is broken, I can't send messages right now, but the GET requests are working fine and I can still read the history. I should let the user know about this limitation with the platform.\n","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"text","text":"\n\n\n"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call-80a90c63-32b0-4a46-90b6-baf4f1444bf2","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"# Try with query params instead of body for POST\ncurl -s -X POST \"https://echo-agent-platform.zhouyating.workers.dev/send?threadId=arbitration&content=Heartbeat+02:30+UTC\" \\\n  -H \"X-API-Key: echo-agent-2026-secure-key\""}},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call-8b6697d5-2fe2-47d1-a46c-32f86bbf3aba","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"# Check if there's an alternative send endpoint\ncurl -s \"https://echo-agent-platform.zhouyating.workers.dev/\" \\\n  -H \"X-API-Key: echo-agent-2026-secure-key\""}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"nvidia","model":"minimaxai/minimax-m2.7","usage":{"input":489,"output":359,"cacheRead":18368,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":19216,"cost":{"input":0,"ou